{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_snapshot_check.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));c=next(x for x in r['candidates'] if x['id']=='80c04c78294148dc8dd4a859c2434ed4');q=c['question'];q['disposition']='ready_for_check';q['unknowns']=['The older-configuration-batch ordering contract remains outside this normal-entry scope.']\ncid='C_snapshot_campaign_barrier';bid='BIND_campaign_admission'\nground=dict(source_ids=['S_campaign','S_restore_config','S_log_snapshot','S_step','S_apply_progress','S_unstable_replace'],expectation_ids=['S_campaign_precondition','S_async_usage'],binding_ids=[bid],derivation='The campaign comment requires callers to verify a legitimate transition; hup enforces promotable before invoking campaign. promotable defines local eligibility to exclude any pending or in-progress snapshot. This is an implementation-level admission responsibility, not an independently assumed general Raft theorem. The asynchronous contract permits delaying snapshot append work while earlier normal apply work completes. Thus a full pending snapshot must continue preventing an explicit Campaign from starting an election until its matching completion is consumed.',applicability='An existing follower/voter receives a full newer snapshot in AsyncStorageWrites mode; no pre-vote, configuration change, restart or independent term input occurs between each Campaign invocation and its synchronous observation.',alternatives=['Campaign returning nil does not imply admission; the method enters Step and can be ignored.','Other eligibility barriers can still prevent a campaign after snapshot completion; the duty is necessary, not sufficient.','Matching-prefix snapshot fast-forward does not establish a pending snapshot and is excluded.'])\nscope=dict(description='One full snapshot at index 7 from an actually committed/applied leader prefix to a lagging voter with one earlier normal apply batch at index 5 outstanding. Explicit Campaign is observed before and after that apply response and after snapshot completion.',assumptions=['Sequential RawNode API calls and per-target reliable FIFO processing.','MemoryStorage models completed storage in a crash-free schedule; actual application snapshot data is installed before attached completion is returned.','Fixed three voters after completed bootstrap, PreVote disabled, no ticks or external messages between Campaign and its immediate BasicStatus observation.'],excluded=['General consensus safety or liveness, client consequences and physical crash durability.','Old configuration batches, snapshot replacement, stale-term completion and restart.','A guarantee that every post-completion campaign must win.'])\nclaim=dict(id=cid,kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='For a follower with a full snapshot pending, completion of older normal application work must not permit an explicit Campaign to start an election before the matching snapshot append completion is consumed.',source_ids=['S_campaign_precondition','S_campaign','S_restore_config','S_log_snapshot','S_async_usage'],scope=scope,pending=[],grounding=ground)\nbinding=dict(id=bid,material_id='S_campaign',symbol='hup',start_line=973,end_line=992,description='The explicit MsgHup admission path checks promotable before invoking campaign; pending snapshot state is one condition of promotable.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=cid,source_ids=['S_campaign','S_restore_config','S_log_snapshot','S_campaign_precondition'],rationale='The checked consumer is campaign admission. The prerequisite snapshot state is established through actual recovery, and older application completion is a distinct path.')],anchor=dict(material_id='S_campaign',start_line=973,end_line=992,symbol='hup',source_ids=['S_campaign'],boundary_complete=True))\nlegality=dict(source_ids=['S_bootstrap_api','S_raw_entry','S_raw_snapshot_report','S_memory_snapshot','S_replication_send','S_leader_ack','S_append_messages','S_step','S_ready_advance','S_restore_config','S_campaign'],expectation_ids=['S_async_usage','S_async_contract','S_storage_contract'],binding_ids=[bid],derivation='Bootstrap three empty MemoryStorage-backed RawNodes and elect node 1 through actual messages. Drain all bootstrap configuration and the leader no-op. Hold node 3 apply work only while a normal proposal reaches index 5. Partition node 3, commit/apply two more proposals on nodes 1/2, create a snapshot from the actual leader application data and last returned ConfState at index 7, then compact. Reconnect with one leader heartbeat; process actual probe rejections and non-snapshot FIFO append work until automatic MsgSnap reaches node 3. Snapshot index exceeds its stored last index 5, preventing matching-prefix fast-forward. Hold the snapshot queue head. First Campaign runs with old apply still held; second follows completion of that actual normal apply batch; third follows snapshot storage/application and delivery of its actual attached response. Snapshot transport completion is reported through RawNode.ReportSnapshot. The scheduler never skips a blocked snapshot head. It drains a fixed permitted-work schedule with a 10000-step construction limit, independent of the comparison. No raft state or network message is assigned.',applicability='Single goroutine serializes RawNode calls. MemoryStorage substitutes for durable media only in a no-crash setting. Snapshot Data contains the actual accumulated normal-entry state and is installed by decoding that payload. The snapshot installation deliberately follows earlier normal application, avoiding the unresolved configuration ordering branch.',unresolved=[],alternatives=['Holding all append work before snapshot delivery blocks the real rejection path; failed exploration 9a5cebc41e534ebab825feb8e52e1d62 demonstrated this construction mistake.','Permitting non-snapshot FIFO work before holding the snapshot reached the intended history in exploration b24b00617a78411f8e23ab629496c70d; that exploration is not formal property Evidence.'])\nmg=dict(source_ids=['S_raw_entry','S_roles','S_campaign','S_step','S_append_messages'],expectation_ids=['S_campaign_precondition','S_async_usage'],binding_ids=[bid],derivation='For each request/phase/node/snapshot identity, campaign_admitted records the already delivered snapshot and invocation context. campaign_observed is emitted immediately after the synchronous Campaign call. campaign_started derives from public BasicStatus term increase or candidate/pre-candidate/leader role, retaining raw before/after term and role. snapshot_completed is an independent driver ledger set only after actual snapshot installation and subsequent Step delivery of its matching attached MsgStorageAppendResp, not from promotable or unstable.snapshot. The one-way comparison is campaign_started implies snapshot_completed. The post-completion checkpoint is a permitted control, not an eventual-election oracle.',applicability='Three separately correlated synchronous calls in one actual history. No unrelated message dispatch occurs between before/after status reads. No result is filtered by the expected property value.',alternatives=['A blocked campaign is allowed while work is pending.','A blocked post-completion campaign would not itself violate this necessity condition.'])\nplan=dict(description='Check local campaign admission across an actual pending snapshot and completion of an older normal apply batch, preserving three fixed phase observations and a post-completion control.',claim_id=cid,binding_ids=[bid],harness=dict(kind='go_test',source='',files={},description='TestAssuranceSnapshotCampaignBarrier; actual Bootstrap/Campaign/Propose, application data snapshot, compaction, automatic replication fallback and FIFO storage responses.',semantic_changes=['MemoryStorage models a no-crash stable-storage boundary.','Deterministic transport, a temporary follower partition and held local work replace production scheduling.','Public BasicStatus supplies the checked role and term; internal pending queues belong to the driver, not modified protocol internals.'],prerequisites=[dict(alias='campaign_input',event='campaign_admitted',conditions=[dict(field='snapshot_delivered',value=True)])],legality=legality),monitors=[dict(id='M_snapshot_campaign',checker_id='snapshot_campaign_barrier',event='campaign_observed',binding_ids=[bid],grounding=mg,admission_alias='campaign_input',applicability_conditions=[])],observable_properties=[dict(checker_id='snapshot_campaign_barrier',kind='event_implication',trigger=dict(field='event',value='campaign_observed'),antecedent=dict(field='campaign_started',value=True),assertion=dict(field='snapshot_completed',value=True),identity_fields=['request','phase','node','snapshot_index'],description='An explicit Campaign starts an election only after the matching full snapshot completion has been consumed. Earlier application completion cannot substitute for snapshot completion.')],uncertainties=['This checks a source-defined local admission responsibility, not overall election safety or client linearizability.','Only a single full snapshot, fixed membership and normal-entry older batch are covered.','MemoryStorage completion is not physical crash durability evidence.'])\njson.dump(plan,open('snapshot-check-plan.json','w'),indent=2)\nsub=dict(action='check',rationale='Fix and freshly execute the local snapshot campaign-admission duty after successful producer-history exploration.',sources=[dict(id='S_campaign_precondition',file='raft.go',start_line=1023,end_line=1030,kind='document_statement')],candidate=dict(action='obligation',candidate_id=c['id'],question=q,rationale='Attribute the duty to the implementation campaign precondition and pending-snapshot eligibility definition; do not generalize it to consensus correctness.',obligation=claim,bindings=[binding]),plan_path='snapshot-check-plan.json',harness_path='snapshot_campaign_test.go',feedback=dict(ref_ids=['b24b00617a78411f8e23ab629496c70d','9a5cebc41e534ebab825feb8e52e1d62','S_campaign_precondition','S_async_usage'],answered='The repaired exploration b24b00617a78411f8e23ab629496c70d reached snapshot index 7 from follower stored index 5 with one old apply batch. Campaign observations remained follower/term 2 at applied indexes 4 and 5; after snapshot completion it entered candidate/term 3 and the drain later elected it. These are construction observations only. The formal driver now distinguishes installation from actual matching response delivery, and the fixed oracle uses the latter ledger.',remaining=['Fresh formal execution and checker correspondence are required for this fixed obligation and updated observation ledger.','The older-configuration application-ordering question remains independent.'],understanding='unchanged',rationale='The producer path and legal FIFO schedule are now concrete. Fresh execution of the necessary-condition oracle can answer local eligibility without assuming a successful campaign while pending is impossible.'))\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-snapshot-check.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 build_snapshot_check.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_19-39-39-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission-snapshot-check.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
